-- title:
--   Ordinary completed stalks of the full-level moduli ring are normal domains
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$, and a nonzero integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite. Assume: `hℓ` and `hM`, that level-$P$ data for $\ell$ (points $P,Q$ on the curve, both killed by $\operatorname{pre}\Psi_\ell$, with the two independence elements units) and $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel data (the polynomials $h$ of the prescribed degree and leading coefficient dividing $\operatorname{pre}\Psi$ suitably, or two-kernel data when $p^k=2$) transport along Weierstrass variable changes; that $\mathcal{G}$ is a family of relative group laws on the projective models of curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras which is chord–tangent (`h𝒢`) and whose unit section is the origin (`h𝒢O`); that $\mathcal{T}$ transports raw Drinfeld pairs at $q$ compatibly with base change and variable change (`h𝒯`); and `hVC`, `hCO`, that variable changes and coefficient homomorphisms are induced by graded ring maps of the projective model rings respecting irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package, with universal point, for the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataPow` (the product of the $\Gamma_0(M')$, level-$\ell$ and Drinfeld-$q$ level components), with $B_0 := P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, and let $x$ be a raw point over $B_0$ whose class is the universal point. Let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a maximal ideal of $B_0$ containing $q$, and $F_0$ a formal group over $B_0/\mathfrak{m}$ whose power series is the formal group law of the reduction of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}$, and assume $F_0$ is ordinary in the sense that its $q$-th iterated series equals a unit times $X^q$. Then the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $B_0$ is an integrally closed domain in which the image of $q$ is nonzero.
--
--   This is the ordinary branch of the normality statement for the completed local rings of the fine moduli ring carrying $\Gamma_0(M') \times \Gamma(\ell) \times \text{Drinfeld-}\Gamma(q)$ level structure, at a point of residue characteristic $q$; in the ordinary case the completion is presented as a power series ring over the coefficient ring with one root adjoined, hence regular of dimension two. It is used in the deduction of flatness and integral closedness of the quotients of the moduli ring by minimal primes over $q$, and in the identification of the completion at an unramified point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isDomain_and_isIntegrallyClosed_adicCompletion_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_X_pow_levelModuliPackageAbs_gamma0Pow.lean

